WEBVTT

00:01.501 --> 00:04.754
THE KUROYURI PARTY

00:11.594 --> 00:14.264
Good evening, my friends!

00:14.806 --> 00:17.434
Members of the electorate!

00:23.398 --> 00:25.400
So you failed again?

00:25.900 --> 00:27.318
My apologies.

00:27.819 --> 00:31.406
Their vigilance towards us
is off the charts.

00:31.656 --> 00:33.324
I'm not surprised.

00:33.908 --> 00:36.578
But I do have a backup plan in place.

00:50.842 --> 00:57.432
YOZAKURA FAMILY

02:14.509 --> 02:18.096
PLAN 8
THE KUROYURI PARTY

02:26.396 --> 02:30.108
<i>Mutsumi asked me
to help her with an errand.</i>

02:30.191 --> 02:32.318
<i>But where are we going
with all this stuff?</i>

02:50.420 --> 02:51.921
Oh, there you are!

02:55.758 --> 02:58.595
It's been a long time, Lady Mutsumi.

02:58.928 --> 03:01.389
I'm counting on you today, Sui!

03:03.099 --> 03:06.019
- You're looking as moronic as ever.
- Eh--

03:06.394 --> 03:07.562
You know him?

03:07.645 --> 03:10.607
We've rubbed shoulders as colleagues.

03:11.524 --> 03:12.525
It's an honor.

03:12.609 --> 03:15.570
That said, I should let you know
that I'm still mad

03:15.653 --> 03:18.948
about the incident with Nanao and Taiyo.

03:19.032 --> 03:20.992
Feel free.
I was only doing my mission.

03:21.826 --> 03:23.536
Anyway, let's get going.

03:23.620 --> 03:25.246
The Hinagiku leader is waiting.

03:27.040 --> 03:28.124
<i>Oh...</i>

03:28.208 --> 03:29.334
Leader?

03:32.003 --> 03:36.883
CABINET OFFICE BUILDING

03:39.719 --> 03:41.429
Taiyo! What are you doing?

03:41.930 --> 03:42.931
Come on!

03:43.014 --> 03:44.724
Eh? Oh!

03:45.475 --> 03:46.476
HINAGIKU

03:49.646 --> 03:50.855
<i>A café?</i>

03:51.606 --> 03:52.899
Welcome.

03:53.566 --> 03:55.735
Three Hinagiku Ultra Super Totally Deluxe

03:55.818 --> 03:58.947
Gigantic Crazy Special
Monster Extreme Caffè Lattes, please.

03:59.447 --> 04:01.783
<i>Did a grade schooler
come up with that name?!</i>

04:02.116 --> 04:03.534
Very good, sir.

04:03.618 --> 04:04.911
<i>It actually exists?!</i>

04:07.163 --> 04:09.332
Enjoy your drinks.

04:10.500 --> 04:11.501
Huh?

04:11.709 --> 04:13.836
Whoa!

04:14.504 --> 04:17.006
300 meters till we reach the lowest level.

04:17.465 --> 04:18.758
We're an intelligence unit

04:18.841 --> 04:21.511
supporting the government
literally behind the scenes.

04:23.638 --> 04:25.765
Welcome to Hinagiku.

04:31.271 --> 04:33.731
We have a little time
before we reach the chief's office.

04:34.190 --> 04:35.942
Drink your latte before it gets cold.

04:36.025 --> 04:37.110
Thanks!

04:37.193 --> 04:39.362
The Hinagiku-let's-skip-the-rest
Extreme Caffè Latte?

04:39.445 --> 04:42.699
And you've got some nerve,
holding Mutsumi like that.

04:42.782 --> 04:44.909
It's dangerous, so I must.

04:44.993 --> 04:47.328
You need to look ahead yourself
or you'll be killed.

04:47.412 --> 04:48.955
What?

04:55.044 --> 04:57.338
These are traps
for both security and training.

04:57.422 --> 05:00.550
Let your guard down and you'll be
ground beef before we reach the bottom.

05:00.883 --> 05:03.928
I only came because I was asked!

05:04.721 --> 05:06.973
That's the entrance
to the chief's office.

05:07.974 --> 05:09.225
Whoa.

05:13.187 --> 05:15.940
Hey, if you don't move out
of the way now, you'll get crushed.

05:20.111 --> 05:21.612
Nice of you to come...

05:22.447 --> 05:23.906
Mr. and Mrs. Yozakura!

05:30.246 --> 05:31.289
Uh?

05:35.168 --> 05:39.213
Can a weakling like you
really keep Mutsumi safe?

05:54.228 --> 05:55.772
Yum!

05:55.855 --> 05:59.567
I can taste
your love and kindness, Mutsumi!

05:59.650 --> 06:03.237
The tea you brought back from
your overseas mission smells divine!

06:03.738 --> 06:06.657
Thanks so much for coming, Mutsumi.

06:06.741 --> 06:08.993
Now I feel motivated for my next mission!

06:09.494 --> 06:10.745
I should be thanking you!

06:10.828 --> 06:12.413
This is such a nice breather for me.

06:12.914 --> 06:16.376
See, Rin's a former classmate
of Big Bro Kyoichiro's,

06:17.001 --> 06:18.628
and she throws tea parties like this

06:18.711 --> 06:20.671
from time to time.

06:22.673 --> 06:25.134
<i>So the errand
was a tea party at Hinagiku?</i>

06:25.635 --> 06:28.930
<i>And her bag... was just full of sweets?</i>

06:29.722 --> 06:32.141
Don't say that
sister-obsessed dirtbag's name around me.

06:32.225 --> 06:34.519
It'll ruin the taste of my cake!

06:34.602 --> 06:37.021
She and Big Bro
are like oil and water.

06:38.189 --> 06:41.317
Because I think anyone
who would shackle this adorable girl

06:41.401 --> 06:42.735
ought to be drawn and quartered!

06:42.819 --> 06:46.823
In this industry full of psychos,
she's like an oasis for my dried-up soul!

06:46.906 --> 06:48.950
Though they are alike
in this particular way!

06:49.534 --> 06:51.619
That's why I wanted you
to marry a guy

06:51.702 --> 06:53.955
capable of protecting you
from that pervert.

06:54.372 --> 06:55.456
But this isn't gonna cut it.

06:55.540 --> 06:57.083
<i>This proximity! I can't take it!</i>

06:57.625 --> 06:59.836
I heard about you from Sui,
you know.

06:59.919 --> 07:01.671
He called you a scumbag turd.

07:02.422 --> 07:05.133
No one speaks in such
a vulgar manner but you, Chief.

07:05.633 --> 07:09.053
All I said was that as a spy,
he's lower than low, excrement.

07:09.387 --> 07:11.013
<i>That's basically the same thing!</i>

07:11.097 --> 07:16.018
That's not true, Rin. Taiyo's soul
is just as strong as Big Bro's.

07:16.102 --> 07:20.314
Well, if you say so,
Mutsumi, it must be so.

07:21.524 --> 07:25.403
<i>That said, have you spoken to him
about...</i>

07:34.620 --> 07:38.666
The only ones capable
of blocking our GPS is Hinagiku.

07:38.749 --> 07:42.879
All right, hand over Mutsumi. Or else...

07:47.758 --> 07:49.093
Oh, please!

07:49.719 --> 07:52.054
So, you decided
to show your face, pervert.

07:52.388 --> 07:54.891
We're in the middle of a tea party.
Get the hell out of here.

07:54.974 --> 07:55.975
Shut up.

07:56.058 --> 07:59.729
Just being in the presence of a vulgar
female gorilla will corrupt Mutsumi.

08:01.772 --> 08:04.609
Male jealousy is so unseemly, isn't it?

08:05.151 --> 08:06.360
Rin Punch!

08:10.490 --> 08:13.618
You really think you can slash me
with those shoddy wires?

08:14.577 --> 08:18.664
How should I butcher and package
that body you're so proud of?

08:27.256 --> 08:29.175
<i>Emergency code
Cherry Blossom Snow!</i>

08:29.258 --> 08:32.637
<i>Everyone in the building,
please evacuate immediately! Repeat...</i>

08:32.720 --> 08:35.014
Hey, this is bad, isn't it?

08:35.640 --> 08:38.684
Come on, why does this always happen?

08:38.768 --> 08:39.936
This always happens?

08:40.019 --> 08:41.145
I'll stop them.

08:41.521 --> 08:43.022
You two head for the emergency exit.

08:43.105 --> 08:44.982
Sui! That's crazy!

08:45.066 --> 08:46.067
It should be me--

08:50.321 --> 08:51.405
Get lost.

08:51.489 --> 08:52.490
You're in the way, Sui.

09:00.373 --> 09:01.374
- Die--
- Die--

09:02.833 --> 09:04.001
<i>Mutsumi?</i>

09:04.502 --> 09:05.711
<i>Move--</i>

09:10.925 --> 09:12.009
Taiyo!

09:20.268 --> 09:21.519
You two...

09:23.563 --> 09:26.357
If either of you cause
any more trouble for everyone...

09:27.942 --> 09:29.694
I'll never speak to you again.

09:34.115 --> 09:38.119
Sorry! Please forgive me, Mutsumi!

09:38.202 --> 09:39.453
Really!

09:40.371 --> 09:43.916
Hey, but you know what?
He's tougher than he looks.

09:44.417 --> 09:46.377
Right? Didn't I say so?

09:46.877 --> 09:48.671
He's my husband, after all.

09:52.049 --> 09:55.428
<i>I see. This one could actually...</i>

09:57.513 --> 10:00.683
Taiyo, I need to speak with you.

10:05.104 --> 10:07.273
Go undercover to investigate a politician?

10:07.356 --> 10:10.943
The Dancing Politician,
Yoshimasa Kuroyuri.

10:11.902 --> 10:14.405
Free education.
Pension normalization.

10:14.488 --> 10:16.115
Reduction of consumer tax.

10:16.198 --> 10:18.951
The one who pulled off
the Kuroyuri Revolution,

10:19.035 --> 10:21.912
the hero of Japan!

10:22.830 --> 10:25.916
That's yours truly,
the leader of the Kuroyuri Party...

10:27.335 --> 10:30.171
Yoshimasa Kuroyuri!

10:30.838 --> 10:32.548
We are...

10:32.632 --> 10:35.760
Kuroyuri! Kuroyuri...

10:36.260 --> 10:37.928
<i>His appearance belies the fact</i>

10:38.012 --> 10:41.641
<i>that he's the politician
with the most momentum right now.</i>

10:42.141 --> 10:46.896
<i>But there's a lot of bloodshed
behind all his achievements.</i>

10:48.356 --> 10:54.028
<i>Fixtures in the political spy rankings,
the triplet spies, Red, Blue, Yellow.</i>

10:56.072 --> 11:00.159
<i>With them as his right-hand men,
he's used bribery, assassination,</i>

11:00.242 --> 11:02.536
<i>every method in the book
to work his way up.</i>

11:03.412 --> 11:08.167
<i>And now he's about to make a major move
ahead of the next general election.</i>

11:08.709 --> 11:11.587
<i>Until now, he's skillfully
deflected any suspicion.</i>

11:12.922 --> 11:16.550
<i>But we confiscated this miniature bomb
in an unrelated case the other day.</i>

11:16.676 --> 11:18.552
<i>It may only have a range of a few meters,</i>

11:18.636 --> 11:23.099
<i>but since it leaves no trace behind,
it's a must-have for assassins overseas.</i>

11:25.309 --> 11:27.561
There are already
several of these at large,

11:27.645 --> 11:31.691
but apparently not even the smuggler
we arrested has seen his customer's face.

11:32.066 --> 11:34.527
But we do have one clue.

11:35.403 --> 11:39.156
<i>What he does remember is the sparkly,
fluffy clothing he glimpsed on-screen</i>

11:39.240 --> 11:41.575
<i>and the heart-shaped sunglasses
his client was wearing.</i>

11:43.202 --> 11:45.162
<i>Bomb, please.</i>

11:45.663 --> 11:47.206
<i>He's totally on-screen!</i>

11:47.581 --> 11:52.044
But this isn't enough for us
to get a warrant for a politician.

11:52.712 --> 11:55.089
Before there are any casualties,

11:55.172 --> 11:58.884
we've got to gain surefire intel
on their bombing plans.

11:59.552 --> 12:01.679
And you want me to take on that mission?

12:02.054 --> 12:03.264
But why?

12:03.889 --> 12:05.725
He's from this country.

12:05.808 --> 12:09.437
He's aware of Hinagiku's existence,
and he's got his guard up against us.

12:09.520 --> 12:13.816
Meaning someone like you, an outsider,
would be hard for him to detect.

12:14.316 --> 12:15.401
And so...

12:16.444 --> 12:17.445
I'm counting on you!

12:19.613 --> 12:20.614
What?

12:25.161 --> 12:26.787
Huh?

12:26.871 --> 12:29.874
You look really great in that, Taiyo!
So cute!

12:29.957 --> 12:32.084
Yeah, it suits you. Wow. Wow.

12:32.168 --> 12:33.961
Hey! You're not even looking!

12:34.044 --> 12:35.796
Wait, why do I have to dress as a woman?

12:35.880 --> 12:39.759
See, the Kuroyuri Party
just posted this help-wanted ad.

12:40.050 --> 12:41.302
NOW HIRING
FEMALE, BLACK HAIR, LONG EYELASHES

12:41.385 --> 12:43.387
It's so specific!
No, that's exactly me!

12:45.222 --> 12:48.225
So many lives have their fate
resting on your shoulders.

12:48.309 --> 12:50.436
Make sure you get that information.

12:50.978 --> 12:52.646
Uh...

12:54.982 --> 12:56.776
THE KUROYURI PARTY

12:56.859 --> 12:58.652
We are...

12:58.819 --> 13:03.073
Kuroyuri! Kuroyuri! Kuroyuri!

13:03.532 --> 13:05.534
Hello, my friends!

13:06.076 --> 13:08.996
Today, I'm going to introduce
a new comrade to you!

13:09.622 --> 13:11.123
Yoko Asada!

13:11.207 --> 13:12.208
Clap!

13:16.420 --> 13:19.006
You must be overwhelmed
by all that cheering.

13:19.423 --> 13:22.218
But you, too,
are part of the hero's family.

13:22.718 --> 13:24.929
So stand tall!

13:25.012 --> 13:27.139
<i>I wanna go home!</i>

13:27.223 --> 13:28.766
Hero, my foot!

13:29.183 --> 13:31.227
The policies you pushed
only widened the gap!

13:31.310 --> 13:33.687
They're evil to the extreme!

13:33.771 --> 13:35.981
Don't let this tyrant oppress the weak!

13:36.357 --> 13:37.983
Who's the real tyrant here?

13:38.067 --> 13:39.443
Get the hell out of here now!

13:52.957 --> 13:54.542
Mr. Kuroyuri!

13:55.751 --> 13:59.380
The anger towards my policies,
the difference in our philosophies...

13:59.463 --> 14:00.756
no matter what shape it takes,

14:00.840 --> 14:04.635
it's the voice of the people,
a shout from the soul...

14:05.094 --> 14:08.889
But... we came here to thwart you...

14:09.974 --> 14:13.310
It's your right as citizens
to have an opinion, no matter what it is.

14:13.811 --> 14:17.565
And it's my mission
to listen to those voices.

14:17.898 --> 14:21.861
Let's continue to have these
fair and open discussions.

14:28.993 --> 14:31.996
Ms. Asada, you go on back to the office.

14:32.079 --> 14:33.455
R-Right.

14:33.747 --> 14:35.624
We are...

14:35.708 --> 14:40.671
Kuroyuri!
Kuroyuri! Kuroyuri!

14:43.382 --> 14:45.759
All right, people.

14:49.555 --> 14:52.600
I thank you for your hard work!

14:53.225 --> 14:57.563
The way you timed
that equipment to fall was spot on, Red!

14:57.646 --> 15:01.233
You made my injuries look
extremely realistic! Well done, Yellow!

15:04.486 --> 15:07.573
Now, then, Blue, how did the public react?

15:07.656 --> 15:09.617
KUROYURI PARTY FAVORABILITY RATING

15:09.700 --> 15:12.661
All right! The online reaction's splendid.

15:13.162 --> 15:15.456
Send this footage
to the commercial networks

15:15.539 --> 15:17.458
to fan the flames even further!

15:18.918 --> 15:22.463
This will cause those foolish citizens
to worship me yet again,

15:22.546 --> 15:27.718
and the pinnacle of this country
will soon be mine!

15:30.304 --> 15:32.723
Let's go with this for our next poster!

15:33.182 --> 15:36.226
<i>I knew it.
That accident was totally staged.</i>

15:36.727 --> 15:38.938
<i>Gaining the people's support
by deceiving them...</i>

15:39.438 --> 15:41.398
<i>He's been stooping to these lows
all this time.</i>

15:41.482 --> 15:42.566
We are...

15:42.650 --> 15:44.735
<i>No way am I going
to let them have their way.</i>

15:46.195 --> 15:48.405
<i>I'm going to expose their plot,
no matter what!</i>

15:48.489 --> 15:50.366
THE KUROYURI PARTY

15:50.449 --> 15:51.450
<i>However...</i>

15:53.869 --> 15:54.870
Ms. Asada.

15:55.412 --> 15:56.830
Are you looking for something?

15:56.914 --> 15:59.541
Oh, no! I'm just organizing a bit!

15:59.875 --> 16:00.876
ACCOUNTING REPORT

16:00.960 --> 16:06.298
<i>Try as I might, I just couldn't
find any information on their crimes.</i>

16:07.967 --> 16:09.259
<i>Far from it.</i>

16:09.510 --> 16:13.806
Let me go! I've never accepted any bribes!
This is a conspiracy!

16:14.765 --> 16:15.766
PARTY DEBATE

16:15.849 --> 16:18.102
Sir, you must offer a rebuttal.

16:19.353 --> 16:20.646
My stomach...

16:21.480 --> 16:24.191
<i>Their heinous activities
continued unabated,</i>

16:24.274 --> 16:27.111
<i>and they kept shifting
the political climate in their favor.</i>

16:28.070 --> 16:34.368
<i>And as the bomb loomed overhead,
I had yet to pin down a single clue.</i>

16:35.160 --> 16:37.246
Our budget proposal passed!

16:37.329 --> 16:39.456
A celebratory dance is in order!

16:39.540 --> 16:41.083
<i>What's going on here?</i>

16:42.376 --> 16:44.294
<i>I'm watching them 24 hours a day,</i>

16:44.378 --> 16:46.922
<i>and they show no signs
of drawing up any plans.</i>

16:47.006 --> 16:50.300
<i>How do they
keep committing crime after crime?</i>

16:52.219 --> 16:57.182
Now, now, Ms. Asada,
you must join in on the fun now and then!

16:57.266 --> 16:58.517
<i>I can't take this!</i>

16:59.226 --> 17:02.730
<i>Why do these guys love to dance so much?</i>

17:03.480 --> 17:07.276
<i>For people who dance every day,
they're terrible at keeping rhythm.</i>

17:12.740 --> 17:13.741
<i>Hey, that's...</i>

17:14.533 --> 17:17.453
<i>Target A,
engineered disappearance complete.</i>

17:18.078 --> 17:21.582
<i>Illegal sale of 30%
of Company B's shares, complete.</i>

17:22.166 --> 17:24.710
<i>This will drain
all of the Tanaka faction's funds.</i>

17:25.377 --> 17:29.298
<i>Well done. That leaves me
with one less enemy group!</i>

17:30.257 --> 17:32.509
<i>Morse code? Of course!</i>

17:32.593 --> 17:35.512
<i>They've been doing this
in the open all along.</i>

17:35.596 --> 17:38.307
<i>When I showed Company C
proof of their tax evasion,</i>

17:38.390 --> 17:40.017
<i>they were happy to switch sides.</i>

17:41.226 --> 17:43.270
<i>Those with guilty consciences
are easy.</i>

17:43.353 --> 17:45.314
<i>They don't require any prodding.</i>

17:46.482 --> 17:51.320
<i>All right, why don't we go over tomorrow's
terrorist bomb attack one final time?</i>

18:01.955 --> 18:04.625
Mr. Kuroyuri, I'm counting on you today.

18:05.125 --> 18:07.044
It's mutual, Deputy Prime Minister.

18:07.753 --> 18:10.172
<i>Many foes
of the Kuroyuri Party,</i>

18:10.255 --> 18:12.007
<i>including the Deputy Prime Minister,</i>

18:12.091 --> 18:14.051
<i>will gather at next week's meeting.</i>

18:15.886 --> 18:18.722
<i>They're all formidable foes
who won't succumb to my maneuvering.</i>

18:18.806 --> 18:21.725
<i>That's why I'm going
to get rid of them right then and there.</i>

18:23.268 --> 18:25.896
<i>We'll plant the bomb underneath the stage.</i>

18:25.979 --> 18:28.816
<i>When the speakers mount the podium,
we'll set it off.</i>

18:30.776 --> 18:33.362
<i>The people nearby will die instantly.</i>

18:33.445 --> 18:37.449
<i>Give me some fake injuries
while also shielding me from the blast.</i>

18:38.242 --> 18:42.162
<i>All right, start the music!</i>

18:47.751 --> 18:49.419
Wh-What was that? Terrorists?

18:49.503 --> 18:51.672
No way, you're overreacting.

18:51.755 --> 18:53.257
It must be the fountain's effect.

18:57.302 --> 18:59.429
<i>I had no time
to disable the bomb...</i>

18:59.888 --> 19:02.850
<i>but luckily, I was able to counteract
the blast in a nearby fountain.</i>

19:04.601 --> 19:06.019
<i>Somehow, I managed to thwart--</i>

19:06.103 --> 19:08.397
Too bad for you.

19:08.480 --> 19:13.152
I didn't mention this yesterday,
but I've got another bomb.

19:14.736 --> 19:17.906
Mr. Taiyo Asano!

19:17.990 --> 19:19.658
Now that I have you
in the palm of my hand,

19:19.741 --> 19:21.994
shall we dance?

19:39.887 --> 19:43.473
Now I've gotten rid
of every last one of them. Huh?

19:46.602 --> 19:47.728
Hey, what's this?

19:47.811 --> 19:48.979
Feels so good!

19:49.062 --> 19:50.856
ANTI-SHOCK JACKET MADE BY SHINZO
FLUFF FLUFF

19:51.523 --> 19:55.027
Shock-resistant jackets? Who the hell...

20:00.157 --> 20:01.241
I see.

20:02.784 --> 20:04.203
Blood-spray pellets, eh?

20:04.870 --> 20:06.496
You're full of ideas, aren't you?

20:07.164 --> 20:10.500
But you should have kept playing dead.

20:10.584 --> 20:13.212
Do you really think you have a chance
when it's four on one?

20:16.673 --> 20:18.342
You thought he was alone?

20:19.051 --> 20:20.135
What--

20:20.385 --> 20:23.889
Yoshimasa Kuroyuri
and Red, Blue, and Yellow...

20:24.640 --> 20:25.933
I'm placing you under arrest.

20:29.144 --> 20:30.854
You worthless fools!

20:30.938 --> 20:33.065
How much did I pay you to--

20:33.398 --> 20:36.860
You are the fool for seeking loyalty
from private-sector spies.

20:36.944 --> 20:40.572
No! I never give up!

20:40.948 --> 20:43.992
No!

20:46.411 --> 20:47.996
<i>Zero casualties as of now.</i>

20:48.497 --> 20:51.250
<i>The three who fled won't be coming back.</i>

20:51.792 --> 20:53.919
<i>Hinagiku will take care
of the crime scene.</i>

20:55.254 --> 20:57.422
<i>Your job is to escort him.</i>

20:57.923 --> 21:01.134
<i>When you arrive at headquarters,
hand him over to the chief.</i>

21:03.011 --> 21:04.805
<i>He might make some suspicious moves.</i>

21:05.222 --> 21:06.223
<i>Watch your back.</i>

21:10.978 --> 21:13.855
He's not making anything
but suspicious moves!

21:13.939 --> 21:15.065
Check it out.

21:15.565 --> 21:16.900
Electric Revolver Yae.

21:17.859 --> 21:19.611
That's a traditional Yozakura weapon.

21:19.695 --> 21:21.405
This is the first time I've ever seen it.

21:21.989 --> 21:26.535
Taiyo Asano. You overcame the loss
of your family in an accident,

21:26.618 --> 21:28.870
and persevered to become a proven member

21:28.954 --> 21:30.914
of the Yozakura family,
their excellent rookie.

21:32.332 --> 21:34.001
I don't know where you dug up all that--

21:34.084 --> 21:36.336
But there's
just one unfortunate thing.

21:36.628 --> 21:39.298
The fact that you really believe
it was an accident.

21:41.633 --> 21:45.178
Hide Asano, Akari Asano, Hikaru Asano...

21:45.679 --> 21:48.724
One rainy day,
they fell off a cliff, car and all.

21:49.558 --> 21:52.477
<i>Your family died instantly,
but you alone survived.</i>

21:52.561 --> 21:54.396
<i>Truly miraculous.</i>

21:54.479 --> 21:55.689
<i>However...</i>

21:56.315 --> 22:01.862
some miracles are the handiwork of man.

22:04.406 --> 22:05.657
What are you talking about?

22:07.784 --> 22:08.785
You...

22:09.411 --> 22:11.788
What do you know about my family?

23:47.884 --> 23:50.887
NEXT TIME
THE FLOWER MEANING OF KUROYURI
